{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773432330,"nonce":"BoD6wbL+I7dxAwXpQi8f2PCcUyA=","title":"push-sync: auth bypass via agent key, spinner delay from scanAll in loop","message":"Two bugs in push-all flow:\n1. Auth never requested — GIT_SSH_COMMAND uses ControlMaster=auto with no identity specified. SSH agent provides id_ed25519_agents (no touch required), bypassing YubiKey entirely.\n2. Spinner delay — scanner.scanAll() is awaited after every per-repo push inside the loop, blocking the next push:repo:progress event by 1-2s per repo.\n\nFix:\n- Add push_ssh_identity setting; enforce with IdentitiesOnly=yes + -i \u003ckey\u003e\n- Pre-auth step: establish ControlMaster to each unique host before any pushes begin\n- Emit push:auth:pending / push:auth:complete SSE events; UI shows touch-key banner\n- Move scanner.scanAll() out of per-repo loop (fire-and-forget after all repos done)","files":null}]}